  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gaza Sings: Young Palestine Raises Its Voice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ESNCM is a specialized music institution that works on a national level in three broad areas. A) Education through regular and community teaching programmes, and supplementary activities including orchestras and ensembles, the Palestine National Music Competition, and publication unit. B) Audience building through festivals, special music events, and a production unit including a state of the art music-recording studio. C) Investing in culture infrastructure: fully equipped branches to deliver advanced music education, the recording studio and the string instruments repair workshop and factory.

Gaza Sings contributes to safeguarding and celebrating Palestinian cultural diversity through raising the voice of young Palestine. It develops the creative capacities of children and youth, empowering them to create and disseminate artistic productions through local and international partnerships, through targeting: 
a) Empowering Gaza Music School to enhance and expand music education (770 students/yr), and foster cultural participation in Gaza (15,000 people).
b) Supporting and promoting productions by young musicians and creative professional (63 productions, 1,500 participants, 150,000 audiences in Palestine and abroad</narrative>
  </description>
